---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
const repo = 'https://github.com/osvanta/bus-log-analyzer';
---
<Base title="Licences" description="Licence of Osvanta Bus Log Analyzer and of the third-party software it uses.">
  <div class="prose">
    <h1>Licences</h1>

    <h2>Osvanta Bus Log Analyzer</h2>
    <p>
      The application's source code is published under the
      <a href={`${repo}/blob/main/LICENSE`}>Mozilla Public License 2.0</a> (MPL-2.0). You may use
      it for any purpose, including commercially, at no cost.
    </p>

    <h2>Third-party software</h2>
    <p>
      The application is built with open-source libraries, among them Python, Qt for Python
      (PySide6), pyqtgraph, NumPy, pandas, asammdf, cantools, canmatrix, python-can and ldfparser.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <a href={`${repo}/blob/main/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md`}>Third-party notices</a>: every library
        shipped, with its version and licence.
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href={`${repo}/tree/main/licenses`}>Licence texts</a>, also in the
        <code>licenses</code> folder of each download.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Names and trademarks</h2>
    <p>
      Names of third-party products, tools and file formats on this site are used only to say what
      the application can read and write, and may be trademarks of their owners. Osvanta is not
      affiliated with, or endorsed by, those owners.
    </p>

    <h2>This website</h2>
    <p>
      The text and images of this website are &copy; Osvanta. The screenshots show a made-up demo
      vehicle, not real data.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
